WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:05.630
Every town across this incredible country

2
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.710
is someone's hometown.

3
00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.720
And we're highlighting as many as we can,

4
00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:12.900
like Boston, Massachusetts,

5
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.600
where attorney and mother of two, Anna Foster calls home

6
00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.700
and get this, she created an organization

7
00:00:19.700 --> 00:00:22.460
that helps budding female entrepreneurs

8
00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:24.410
in her local area.

9
00:00:24.410 --> 00:00:25.363
Take a look.

10
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:28.610 line:15%
Hi Drew, it's Anna Foster

11
00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:31.500 line:15%
and I am standing in front of WBZ-TV

12
00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:34.020
in my hometown of Boston.

13
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.950 line:15%
I love Boston because it's rich in culture.

14
00:00:36.950 --> 00:00:40.490 line:15%
It's rich in community, and it's rich in innovation.

15
00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:42.600 line:15%
I want to show you around Boston.

16
00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:43.780
So come with me Drew.

17
00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.283
We're gonna have a great time.

18
00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:49.180 line:15%
Right now we're at the Seaport area of Boston

19
00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:52.340 line:15%
and right at the site of the Boston Tea Party.

20
00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.680 line:15%
I loved this area as I was growing up.

21
00:00:54.680 --> 00:00:56.280
It didn't look exactly like this,

22
00:00:56.280 --> 00:00:59.000
but as you can see, it's thriving and flourishing.

23
00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:01.270 line:15%
It has the water, it has the boats,

24
00:01:01.270 --> 00:01:05.100 line:15%
it has great restaurants and amazing small businesses.

25
00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:07.660 line:15%
Hope you can visit the Seaport area of Boston one day.

26
00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:08.623
You'll love it.

27
00:01:10.590 --> 00:01:12.430
So we're right here in City Hall Plaza

28
00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:14.020
in the heart of Boston,

29
00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.830 line:15%
and I have a special guest with me.

30
00:01:16.830 --> 00:01:18.000 line:15%
Drum roll...

31
00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:20.050 line:15%
the mayor of Boston.

32
00:01:20.050 --> 00:01:23.440 line:15%
Mayor Kim Janey is right here standing next to me.

33
00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:24.950
I'm so excited.

34
00:01:24.950 --> 00:01:27.130
Mayor Janey, tell us about Boston

35
00:01:27.130 --> 00:01:28.880
and why you love this city.

36
00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:30.610 line:15%
Anna, thank you so much,

37
00:01:30.610 --> 00:01:33.020 line:15%
and a shout out to everyone watching.

38
00:01:33.020 --> 00:01:34.500 line:15%
I love my city.

39
00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.960 line:15%
This is the city that I'm born and raised in.

40
00:01:36.960 --> 00:01:38.460 line:15%
I am a city girl.

41
00:01:38.460 --> 00:01:40.790 line:15%
Boston is a great world-class city,

42
00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:43.470
a city of innovation, a city of firsts.

43
00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.080
We are the birthplace of America,

44
00:01:45.080 --> 00:01:47.660
the birthplace of public education.

45
00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.240
First library, the best hospitals in the world,

46
00:01:50.240 --> 00:01:53.860
the best universities, public space, beautiful parks,

47
00:01:53.860 --> 00:01:56.570
and I'm just so grateful and honored to serve

48
00:01:56.570 --> 00:01:59.800
as the first woman mayor, the first black mayor of Boston.

49
00:01:59.800 --> 00:02:01.100
It is amazing.

50
00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:01.933
Wonderful.

51
00:02:01.933 --> 00:02:05.140
Thank you Madam Mayor Kim Janey.

52
00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:06.480
Well Drew, that's a little bit

53
00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.010
about my hometown of Boston.

54
00:02:08.010 --> 00:02:09.560
I cannot wait for you to visit.

55
00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:10.393
See you soon.

56
00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:13.010
Thanks, Anna.

57
00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:14.580
Boston is wicked cool.

58
00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:17.400
I know, I'm sorry, I had to, but I really do love it.

59
00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.050
I mean, I'll never forget the memories

60
00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:20.580
of being with the Red Sox as

61
00:02:20.580 --> 00:02:22.390
they broke the curse of the Bambino,

62
00:02:22.390 --> 00:02:25.060
while we filmed a movie called Fever Pitch.

63
00:02:25.060 --> 00:02:26.810
And don't even get me started

64
00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:29.250
about Legal Sea Foods clam chowder.

65
00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:30.550
Oh!

66
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.812
I'll see you soon, hopefully.

67
00:02:32.812 --> 00:02:35.312
(theme music)

